    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1147">

                <pb facs="0820" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/73.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Miller to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-21T20:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Constitutionalist forces have troops in Panuco and American companies are sending
                    their American employees to work in fields; suggest oil workers be warned not to
                    return until assured of employment, especially as Aguila Company and Corona
                    Company, account instructions from London, do not wish to employ Americans in
                    oil fields under present conditions and further state do not need them as field
                    work will be shut down to large extent for Aguila Company especially.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
